The supplied excerpt reports only qualitative outcomes. It states that the POMO shared baseline produces zero-mean advantages, reduces policy-gradient variance compared with greedy-rollout baselines, is more efficient because it avoids separate critic or cloned-policy forward passes, and makes training more resistant to premature convergence or local minima. No quantitative objective values, optimality gaps, inference times, baseline comparisons, or statistical significance are provided in the excerpt.
