The paper evaluates a large-scale VRP method built around TTPL/LLM-AHD, in which a TTPL-designed projection is applied to a constructive solver reported as LEHD and then augmented with Multi-View Decision Fusion and a 1,000-iteration RRC refinement procedure. The method is inference-time rather than a progressive training scheme: it uses greedy construction or sampling to build solutions, applies the designed projection, fuses multiple decision views, and refines solutions with RRC. This is related to the proposed ICAM research plan because it targets the same problem of improving TSP/CVRP solution quality at large scales, but it is not the proposed Stage 1 warm-up, Stage 2 varying-scale, or Stage 3 top-k elite training approach; it is closer to a test-time projection/refinement baseline or complement for large-scale evaluation.
[results]
On synthetic TSP instances, the method with purely greedy construction outperforms other greedy constructive methods on most scales except TSP1K; with RRC for 1000 iterations it is best on all TSP scales and reports optimality-gap reductions of 61.11%, 75.59%, 56.2%, 69.61%, and 68.29% on TSP1K, 5K, 10K, 50K, and 100K relative to the leading alternative. On synthetic CVRP, greedy sampling is best on all scales except CVRP1K; with RRC it surpasses all baselines and reports optimality-gap reductions of 53.98%, 85.99%, 86.20%, and 88.37% on CVRP5K, 10K, 50K, and 100K. On TSPLIB/CVRPLIB, TTPL alone achieves 5.80% overall TSP gap and 13.19% overall CVRP gap; TTPL-MVDF achieves 3.88% TSP and 10.97% CVRP; TTPL-MVDF with RRC1000 achieves 1.37% TSP and 7.50% CVRP, solving 33/33 TSPLIB and 14/14 CVRPLIB instances. The best competing benchmark values reported are INViT greedy at 11.04% TSP and 20.49% CVRP, and LEHD RRC1000 at 7.37% TSP and 11.04% CVRP.
[context]
Experiments use TSP/CVRP instances at 1K, 5K, 10K, 50K, and 100K nodes for synthetic evaluation, and TSPLIB/CVRPLIB benchmark groups with 1K<n≤5K and n>5K for TSP and 1K<n≤7K and n>7K for CVRP. The reported hardware is a single NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3090 GPU with 24GB memory. The main refinement setting is RRC with 1000 iterations, and inference uses greedy construction or greedy sampling. Some baselines report OOM or incomplete solved counts, while the TTPL-MVDF RRC1000 setting reports full solved counts. No statistical significance tests are reported in the provided excerpt.
