On TSP, UDC-x50 with alpha=50 achieved objective 16.78, gap 1.58 percent, time 4m at 500 nodes; 23.53, 1.78 percent, 8m at 1000 nodes; and 33.26, 2.49 percent, 15m at 2000 nodes. UDC-x2 greedy achieved 16.94, 2.53 percent, 20s; 23.79, 2.92 percent, 32s; and 34.14, 5.19 percent, 23s. ICAM achieved 16.65, 0.77 percent, 38s at 500 nodes; 23.49, 1.58 percent, 1m at 1000 nodes; and 34.37, 5.93 percent, 3.8m at 2000 nodes. POMO achieved 20.19, 22.19 percent, 1m at 500 nodes; 32.50, 40.57 percent, 8m at 1000 nodes; and 50.89, 56.85 percent, 10m at 2000 nodes. ELG achieved 17.18, 4.00 percent, 2.2m at 500 nodes; 24.78, 7.18 percent, 13.7m at 1000 nodes; and 36.14, 11.37 percent, 14.2m at 2000 nodes. GLOP achieved 16.88, 2.19 percent, 1.5m at 500 nodes; 23.84, 3.12 percent, 3.5m at 1000 nodes; and 33.71, 3.89 percent, 9m at 2000 nodes. TAM achieved 16.94, 2.55 percent, 32m at 500 nodes; 23.77, 2.79 percent, 32m at 1000 nodes; and 33.35, 2.76 percent, 14m at 2000 nodes. Attn-MCTS achieved 16.97, 2.69 percent, 6m at 500 nodes; 23.86, 3.20 percent, 12m at 1000 nodes; and 33.42, 2.99 percent at 2000 nodes. LKH3 reference objectives were 16.52, 23.12, and 32.45. On CVRP, UDC-x50 achieved 38.34, 3.01 percent, 7.7m at 500 nodes; 43.48, 1.11 percent, 14m at 1000 nodes; and 60.94, 1.55 percent, 23m at 2000 nodes. UDC-x250 achieved 37.99, 2.06 percent, 35m at 500 nodes; 43.00 with time 1.2h at 1000 nodes; and 60.01 with time 2.15h at 2000 nodes, with the extracted table not showing a clear gap value for the last two cells. ICAM achieved 37.49, 0.69 percent, 42s at 500 nodes; 43.07, 0.16 percent, 26s at 1000 nodes; and 61.34, 2.21 percent, 3.7m at 2000 nodes. ELG achieved 38.34, 2.99 percent, 2.6m at 500 nodes and 43.58, 1.33 percent, 15.6m at 1000 nodes. GLOP-G achieved 42.45, 11.73 percent, 2.4m at 500 nodes; 45.90, 6.74 percent, 2m at 1000 nodes; and 63.02, 5.01 percent, 2.5m at 2000 nodes. TAM achieved 46.3, 7.67 percent, 4m at 1000 nodes and 64.8, 7.97 percent, 9.6m at 2000 nodes. LKH3 reference objectives were 37.23, 46.40, and 64.90. Overall, ICAM is faster and very competitive at 500 and 1000 nodes, while UDC-x50 and UDC-x250 improve large-scale gaps at higher inference cost. No statistical significance tests are reported in the extracted section.
