[results]
On TSP100, the method produced average length 7.7608 with a reported gap of -0.0011% and a table time entry of 5.68 minutes plus an additional 1.11 minute component. On TSP200, it produced length 10.7289 with gap 0.0918%, and the runtime is reported as 0.56 minutes plus 5.21 minutes. For larger instances, the paper reports gaps of 0.8394% on TSP500 and 1.1770% on TSP1000. On small instances with n=20, 50, and 100, gaps were -0.00009%, -0.002%, and -0.00011%, respectively, attributed to rounding. The table gaps are relative to the Concorde reference row rather than to LKH3, so they are not directly identical to the proposed method's LKH3-based gap metric. Compared with learning baselines, the method was reported to outperform existing learning baselines on TSP200, TSP500, and TSP1000, while classical solvers remained stronger or competitive on TSP200 in the table: LKH3 had gap 0.0040%, Gurobi had gap -0.1446%, and Concorde had gap 0.0000%.
