[context]
The experimental hardware is a 12-core Intel Xeon Platinum 8255C CPU and an NVIDIA RTX 3090 GPU. TSP evaluation includes uniformly sampled TSP500, TSP1K, TSP10K, and TSP100K instances, cross-distribution test instances, and 49 TSPLIB symmetric EUC2D instances under 1000 nodes normalized to the unit square. CVRP evaluation includes generated CVRP1K, CVRP2K, CVRP5K, and CVRP7K test sets of 100 instances each plus several large-scale CVRPLIB instances. PCTSP evaluation uses generated PCTSP500, PCTSP1K, and PCTSP5K instances with prize sampling parameters K_n equal to 9, 12, and 20. Baselines are chosen to have adjustable runtime so they can be matched to GLOP. This context is relevant to the proposed ICAM plan because both approaches test whether a learned routing solver remains effective beyond the primary generated instance distributions, but the paper excerpt lacks the numerical cross-distribution evidence needed to compare directly with ICAM's expected robustness.
